WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.520
One command runs the whole demo.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.165
It loads prices for Claude tokens, creates a customer on a test clock, and sends ten AI calls.

3
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.155
Then it moves the clock a month and builds the invoice. Here's what it made.

4
00:00:18.003 --> 00:00:22.547
These are the prices it loaded: each Claude model, priced per token type.

5
00:00:23.603 --> 00:00:28.211
Here's the customer it created, on a test clock, with a subscription to that plan.

6
00:00:30.945 --> 00:00:33.761
Its AI calls show up as usage, day by day.

7
00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:40.155
The test clock moved a month forward, so the period closed.

8
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:49.100
And the invoice: one line per model and token type, five dollars seventy-three in total.

9
00:00:53.094 --> 00:00:59.494
Finally, your margin: what you billed against what the model provider charged. Fifty-one point nine percent.

10
00:01:00.301 --> 00:01:03.501
Run the same demo on your machine with the commands below.

